 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+
+### Sports
+
+- **MMA and Formula 1 join the Sports tab as fixture feeds.** MMA reads API-Sports' `/fights` (two fighters on a card, in a weight class, with the finish method instead of a score) and Formula 1 reads `/races` by season, filtered to the day (a Grand Prix at its circuit, with the session instead of a score). Both are their own API-Sports products on their own hosts, so they need their own keys - `mma:...` / `formula-1:...` in `apiSportsKeys`, or a bare key from a plan that covers them - and MMA joins the default-enabled sports. With no key for them the board stays guide-only for those sports, as it already was.
+- **MotoGP, NASCAR, IndyCar, WEC, WRC and Formula E join as guide-only sports.** API-Sports sells no product for any of them, so there is no feed to give them a host - their events come off the guide like golf and boxing already do, with their own chips, icons and keywords (`ufc`, `mma`, `bellator`, `pfl`, `one championship`, `motogp`, `nascar`, `indycar`, `wec`, `wrc`, `formula e`). MotoGP no longer files under the Formula 1 chip, including "MotoGP Qualifying", which used to lose to Formula 1's own "qualifying" keyword.
+- **Event rows hide the score boxes.** A fight or a race has no score to show, so the row shows the two names and the card or series line instead of a pair of "–" boxes.
+
 ## 7.1
 
 ### Player
